233 - Christ, Whose Glory Fills the Skies
 / 
Key: D
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 233
Topic: Jesus Christ - 

Verse 1:
[D]Christ, whose [G]glory [D]fills the [A]skies,
[Bm]Christ, the [A/C#]true, [D]the [G]only [D]light,
[D]Sun of [A]Righteousness, [A7/C#]arise,
[D]triumph [Bm]o'er [F#m]the [G]shades [F#m]of [Bm]night;
[G]Dayspring [A]from [Bm]on [Em]high, be [F#m]near;
[Bm/D]Daystar, [A/C#]in [D]my [G]heart [A]appear.

Verse 2:
[D]Dark and [G]cheerless [D]is the [A]morn
[Bm]unaccompanied [G]by [A]thee;
[D]joyless [A]is [D]the [G/B]day's [A7/C#]return,
[D]till [Bm]thy [F#m]mercy's [Em]beams [F#m]I [Bm]see;
[G]till they [A]inward [Em]light impart,
[Bm/D]cheer my [A/C#]eyes [D]and [G]warm [A]my [D]heart.

Verse 3:
[D]Visit [G]then [A7/E]this [D]soul of [A]mine;
[Bm]pierce the [A/C#]gloom [D]of [G]sin [A]and [D]grief;
[D]fill me, [A]Radiancy [A7/C#]divine,
[D]scatter [F#m]all [G]my [Em]unbelief;
[G]more and [A]more [Bm]thyself [Em]display,
[Bm/D]shining [A/C#]to [D]the [G]perfect [D]day.
